Feature: Transition
  The transition changes a hover into forward flight, and back. In the first one, the wing
  motors tilt forward while the plane speeds up, and the wing takes the weight. In the
  second one, the wing motors tilt up while the plane slows down, and the rotors take the
  weight. The plane keeps its height through both.

  Expectation: CRUISE changes a hover into forward flight
    Given the flight is hovering
    When the operator switches to forward flight
    Then the flight is cruising
    And the autopilot mode is CRUISE
    And the height above home is at least 10 m

  Expectation: QLOITER changes forward flight back into a hover
    Given the flight is cruising
    When the operator switches to hover
    Then the flight is hovering
    And the autopilot mode is QLOITER
    And the height above home is at least 10 m
